Royal Archer Community Code of Conduct
Royal Archer is a creative and editorial studio built on respect, clarity, and collaboration.
This Code of Conduct outlines the expectations for everyone who participates in this project
— including contributors, reviewers, maintainers, and community members.

Our goal is to create a space where creativity thrives, ideas are welcomed, and every contributor feels valued.

🌟 1. Our Core Values
Royal Archer is guided by:

Kindness — We treat each other with patience, empathy, and respect.

Craftsmanship — We care about quality, clarity, and thoughtful work.

Integrity — We act honestly and honor our commitments.

Collaboration — We build together, not against each other.

Inclusivity — We welcome diverse voices, backgrounds, and perspectives.

Growth — We learn, improve, and support each other’s development.

These values shape how we communicate, create, and collaborate.

🤝 2. Expected Behavior
All participants are expected to:

Communicate with respect and professionalism

Offer constructive, thoughtful feedback

Listen actively and consider other viewpoints

Ask questions when unsure

Credit others for their work and ideas

Follow project guidelines and maintain consistency

Support a welcoming environment for newcomers

Uphold the mission and tone of Royal Archer

We build a community where everyone feels safe to contribute.

🚫 3. Unacceptable Behavior
The following behaviors are not tolerated:

Harassment, discrimination, or abusive language

Personal attacks or insults

Dismissive or hostile communication

Plagiarism or misrepresentation of work

Sharing private information without consent

Disruptive or intentionally harmful actions

Introducing malicious code or unsafe practices

Using the Royal Archer brand for unauthorized commercial purposes

Violations may result in warnings, PR rejections, or removal from the project.

🛠️ 4. Collaboration Standards
To maintain a healthy creative and technical environment:

Keep discussions focused and relevant

Provide clear explanations for decisions or changes

Respect the project’s editorial voice and brand identity

Follow the contribution workflow described in CONTRIBUTING.md

Seek alignment before making major changes

Accept feedback with openness and professionalism

We aim for clarity, not conflict.

📣 5. Reporting Issues
If you experience or witness behavior that violates this Code of Conduct:

Open an Issue describing the concern, or

Contact the project owner privately if the matter is sensitive

All reports will be handled respectfully and confidentially.

🔐 6. Project Governance
Until a formal co‑ownership agreement is established:

The project owner (Galina B. Nelson) has final authority on decisions

Maintainers may be appointed to assist with reviews and guidance

Contributors are encouraged to participate in discussions and planning

Governance is collaborative, but guided.

🌱 7. Commitment to Growth
We believe in continuous improvement — of the platform, the craft, and the community.
Mistakes are part of learning.
We approach them with patience, humility, and a willingness to grow.

💬 8. Thank You
Thank you for helping build Royal Archer with care and integrity.
Your contributions — technical, editorial, creative, or organizational
— help shape a platform where stories and tools are crafted with purpose.

Together, we create something meaningful.
